@startuml DeleteTask
title Week 9 — Delete confirmation (OK and Cancel)
actor User
boundary "Delete button / bound onDelete callback" as UI
participant "controller: TodoController" as Controller
participant "proxy: ConfirmDeleteProxy" as Proxy
boundary "Browser confirm dialog" as Confirm
participant "logging: LoggingTodoServiceDecorator" as Logging
participant "real: TodoService" as Service
participant "storage: StorageGroup" as Group
participant "list: LocalStorageHandler" as List
participant "archive: ArchiveStorageHandler" as Archive
participant "renderer: TodoRenderer" as Renderer

User -> UI : click Delete
UI -> Controller : deleteTask(id) via bound callback
activate Controller
Controller -> Proxy : deleteTask(id)
activate Proxy
Proxy -> Confirm : confirm("Delete this task?")
Confirm -> User : display OK / Cancel
User --> Confirm : choose
Confirm --> Proxy : boolean choice
alt user chooses OK
  Proxy -> Logging : deleteTask(id)
  activate Logging
  Logging -> Service : deleteTask(id)
  activate Service
  Service -> Service : filter task from active array
  Service -> Group : save(tasks)
  activate Group
  Group -> List : save(tasks)
  List --> Group : todo-tasks replaced
  Group -> Archive : save(tasks)
  Archive --> Group : unseen IDs appended; existing records retained
  Group --> Service : undefined
  deactivate Group
  Service --> Logging : undefined
  deactivate Service
  Logging --> Proxy : undefined
  deactivate Logging
else user chooses Cancel
  note right of Proxy
    No call reaches the decorated service.
    Neither storage key is changed.
  end note
end
Proxy --> Controller : undefined
deactivate Proxy
Controller -> Renderer : render(service-compatible object)
activate Renderer
Renderer --> Controller : current task list displayed
deactivate Renderer
Controller --> UI : undefined
deactivate Controller

note over Controller, Renderer
  The existing controller requests rendering after either result.
  On Cancel, it displays the same unchanged task list.
  On OK, the removed task stays absent after reload,
  and its first-saved record remains in todo-archive.
end note
@enduml
